bing: 736 m"]]]] [:div {:class "description"} [:p {} "The favorite was East German " [:a {:href "/athletes/97058"} "Frank-Peter Roetsch"] " who had won three of the last four seasonal World Cups, and was World Champion in both individual events in 1987. His biggest challenge was expected to come from Soviet biathlete " [:a {:href "/athletes/95344"} "Valery Medvedtsev"] ", winner of both events at the 1986 World Championships. Medvedtsev went off 26th with Roetsch having start number 43. None of the leaders had clean shooting rounds, but Roetsch missed three targets to Medvedtsev’s two. However, it didn’t matter because of Roetsch’s superior skiing speed, which brought him home for the gold medal in 56:33.3. As expected, Medvedtsev was second, finishing 21.3 seconds down to Roetsch. The bronze medal went to Italy’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/96235"} "Johann Passler"] ", who had been third in the sprint at the 1985 World Championships and would finish third in the 1987-88 World Cup race."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "Adjusted Time"] [:th {} "Misses"] [:th {} "Skiing"] [:th {} "Shooting 1 Misses"] [:th {} "Shooting 1"] [:th {} "Shooting 2 Misses"] [:th {} "Shooting 2"] [:th {} "Shooting 3 Misses"] [:th {} "Shooting 3"] [:th {} "Shooting 4 Misses"] [:th {} "Shooting 4"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/97058"} "Frank-Peter Roetsch"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/GDR"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/GDR.png"}] "GDR"]] [:td {} "56:33.3"] [:td {} "3"] [:td {} "53:33.3 (1)"] [:td {} "1"] [:td {} "– (–)"] [:td {} "1"] [:td {} "– (–)"] [:td {} "0"] [:td {} "– (–)"] [:td {} "1"] [:td {} "– (–)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athl